From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] actions: handlebuttonevents: respect session inhibitors on lid close

PowerDevil bypasses the policy agent when it handles the lid switch: the
trigger is marked explicit, so an InterruptSession inhibitor (the Plasma
Mobile Caffeine quick setting, or org.freedesktop.PowerManagement.Inhibit)
does not stop the configured Sleep or Hibernate action.

Check the policy agent before suspending. When the session is inhibited,
turn the display off instead and leave the system running.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
---
 daemon/actions/bundled/handlebuttonevents.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/actions/bundled/handlebuttonevents.cpp b/daemon/actions/bundled/handlebuttonevents.cpp
--- a/daemon/actions/bundled/handlebuttonevents.cpp
+++ b/daemon/actions/bundled/handlebuttonevents.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <PowerDevilProfileSettings.h>
 #include <powerdevil_debug.h>
 #include <powerdevilcore.h>
+#include <powerdevilpolicyagent.h>
 
 #include <QAction>
 
@@ -156,6 +157,14 @@ void HandleButtonEvents::onLidClosedChanged(bool closed)
             return;
         }
 
+        if ((m_lidAction == PowerDevil::PowerButtonAction::Sleep ||
+             m_lidAction == PowerDevil::PowerButtonAction::Hibernate) &&
+            PowerDevil::PolicyAgent::instance()->requirePolicyCheck(PowerDevil::PolicyAgent::InterruptSession) != PowerDevil::PolicyAgent::None) {
+            qCDebug(POWERDEVIL) << "Lid action inhibited by an active session inhibitor, turning off the screen";
+            triggerAction(u"DPMSControl"_s, u"TurnOff"_s);
+            return;
+        }
+
         processAction(m_lidAction);
     } else {
         // When we restore the keyboard brightness before waking up, we shouldn't conflict
